          "text": "Health anxiety regarding epilepsy and brain pathology"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Recent focal seizure events"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Over approximately the past 3 weeks, focal events have become mildly more frequent. Three events occurred last week. The patient describes a weird feeling and jerking of the right arm and face, lasting 30–60 seconds, with awareness preserved, hearing others, and difficulty speaking or speech arrest. He feels tired for a few minutes afterward without prolonged confusion. His mother says these are the same as his usual events, just somewhat more frequent."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Recent seizure-associated findings"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For the recent events, no loss of consciousness, generalized tonic-clonic activity, tongue bite, incontinence, or injury was reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "History of generalized tonic-clonic seizure"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Last generalized tonic-clonic seizure was approximately 8 months ago."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported seizure triggers and sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Poor sleep for approximately 1 month due to worry and lying awake thinking about his brain. Increased energy drink use, 2–3 cans per day, with a new brand."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported pertinent neurologic and systemic negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No persistent weakness, speech change, or vision loss; no new severe headache, fever, neck stiffness, or recent head trauma. No alcohol or illicit drug use reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Telehealth phone examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Speaking in full sentences and mildly anxious; oriented and chatting appropriately. No obvious dysarthria, word-finding problem, or confusion on brief phone screen. No physical examination or vital signs obtained."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Medication adherence and dose timing reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mother manages a Webster pack and believes adherence is greater than 95%. Medications are unchanged; occasional evening doses are 1–2 hours late."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported health anxiety"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding anxiety about brain health, frequent searching online about seizures, cancer, and stroke, and repeated requests for MRI every few months. The patient expressed fear that his brain is getting worse and concern about status epilepticus going unnoticed. No suicidal ideation reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported history of brain lesions associated with tuberous sclerosis"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mother recalls prior 'brain tumours'; cortical tubers or SEGA are queried. Previously followed at a tertiary centre."
      }
    },
    {
